Fix the dead fling at its source: emit Phase::Began at the start of a touch scroll.

This is the root cause behind the split-controller symptom the diagnostics found,
and it is one line of missing state.

The WPE touch gesture recogniser emitted every scroll event of a flick with
WebWheelEvent::Phase::Changed and the terminal event with Phase::Ended - it never
emitted Phase::Began. But the scrolling tree only latches a gesture to a node when
isGestureStart() is true, and isGestureStart() is Began || MayBegin. With no Began,
ScrollingTreeLatchingController::nodeDidHandleEvent()'s shouldLatch() never fired, so
the gesture was never latched and every wheel event was hit-tested independently.

Device-traced on franceinfo.fr with per-controller logging (ctrl=%p):

  ctrl=0x70c6def4e0  wheel in: delta=0,-60  ... historySize=9..20   (motion events)
  ctrl=0x70c5224740  wheel in: delta=0,0 endOfNonMomentum=1 historySize=0  (Ended)
  -> SINGLE-SAMPLE motion=0 -> velocity 0,0 (NO MOMENTUM)

The motion events accumulated one controller's velocity history while the Ended
event - which arms the kinetic fling - landed on a different controller with an
empty history, so the fling computed from a single sample and the page stopped
dead. The un-latched motion controller never received an Ended event, so its
history was never consumed either (visible as historySize persisting across
gestures). This only manifested on pages with more than one scrollable node
reachable under the touch point, i.e. heavy real sites, never a trivial page.

Fix: send the first scroll event of each gesture with Phase::Began (tracked by a
per-gesture flag reset on touch-down). Latching then binds the whole gesture -
Began, the Changed motion stream, and the Ended terminator, all of which route to
the latched node via useLatchedEventElement() - to one scrolling node. The fling
arms on the node that actually accumulated the motion, with full velocity history.

Complementary to webkit-wheel-coalesce-phase-split.patch: that stops distinct
phases from being merged into one event; this ensures the gesture has a start
phase to latch on in the first place. Both are needed.

diff -ruN a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/libwpe/TouchGestureController.cpp b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/libwpe/TouchGestureController.cpp
--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/libwpe/TouchGestureController.cpp	2026-07-20 21:14:37.645043293 +0000
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/libwpe/TouchGestureController.cpp	2026-07-20 21:15:24.135312113 +0000
@@ -73,6 +73,7 @@
         m_start = { true, touchPoint->time, touchPoint->x, touchPoint->y };
         m_offset = { touchPoint->x, touchPoint->y };
         m_xAxisLockBroken = m_yAxisLockBroken = false;
+        m_axisGestureStarted = false;
         g_touchMotionsIn = 0;
         g_axisEventsOut = 0;
         break;
@@ -105,7 +106,16 @@
         case GesturedEvent::Axis:
         {
             AxisEvent generatedEvent;
-            generatedEvent.phase = WebWheelEvent::Phase::Changed;
+            // The first scroll event of a gesture must be Phase::Began so the scrolling
+            // tree latches the whole gesture (motion events and the terminal Ended
+            // event alike) to a single node. Upstream WPE only ever emitted Changed,
+            // so isGestureStart() was never true, latching never engaged, and each
+            // event was hit-tested independently — device-traced on franceinfo.fr,
+            // the motion events built one controller's velocity history while the
+            // Ended event armed a different, empty controller, so the fling saw one
+            // sample and the page stopped dead. See webkit-touch-gesture-began-phase.patch.
+            generatedEvent.phase = m_axisGestureStarted ? WebWheelEvent::Phase::Changed : WebWheelEvent::Phase::Began;
+            m_axisGestureStarted = true;
 
 #if WPE_CHECK_VERSION(1, 5, 0)
             generatedEvent.event.base = {
diff -ruN a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/libwpe/TouchGestureController.h b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/libwpe/TouchGestureController.h
--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/libwpe/TouchGestureController.h	2026-07-20 21:14:59.131167355 +0000
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/libwpe/TouchGestureController.h	2026-07-20 21:15:05.360203379 +0000
@@ -86,6 +86,11 @@
 
     bool m_xAxisLockBroken { false };
     bool m_yAxisLockBroken { false };
+    // True once this gesture has emitted its first axis (scroll) event. The first is
+    // sent with Phase::Began so the scrolling tree latches the gesture to one node;
+    // without it every event hit-tests independently and a flick splits across nodes,
+    // killing the kinetic fling. See webkit-touch-gesture-began-phase.patch.
+    bool m_axisGestureStarted { false };
 };
 
 } // namespace WebKit
